@startuml
title Component Diagram - Zero-Trust Secure Messenger

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor User

package "Client (Trusted Boundary)" #LightGreen {
  component "Web Client (UI)" as UI
  component "Crypto Module" as Crypto
  component "Local Storage (IndexedDB)" as LS

  note right of LS
    Encrypted Private Key
    - AES-GCM(passphrase)

    Session Cache
    - Encrypted messages

    Public Keys
    - Contacts

    Draft Messages
    - Plaintext (local only)
  end note
}

package "Server (Untrusted / Zero-Trust)" #LightCoral {
  component "Auth Service" as Auth
  component "Message Router\n(WebSocket)" as Router
  database "Database" as DB
}

User --> UI : User interaction
UI --> Crypto : encrypt / decrypt\nsign / verify
Crypto --> LS : store encrypted data

UI --> Auth : HTTPS (REST)
UI --> Router : WSS (WebSocket)

Auth --> DB : public keys only
Router --> DB : ciphertext + metadata

note bottom
⚠️ Private keys never leave client unencrypted
🔒 Encryption occurs before network transmission
📊 Server stores ciphertext only
end note

@enduml
